IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sgi-capacity`

-- Tests for sgi-capacity.l4 (ss 23 and 24). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion.
-- A function answers JUST TRUE (the section's test is met), JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words) or NOTHING (the text does not say).

§ `s 23(1)(a): full capacity, subject to this Act, other written law and the constitution`

-- "a company has full capacity to carry on or undertake any business or activity, do any act or enter into any transaction": no limit applies, so yes.
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each of the three "Subject to" limits, alone: the text names no outcome, so NOTHING (never FALSE).
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- All three limits at once.
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(a) the company has full capacity to carry on or undertake the business or activity, do the act or enter into the transaction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23(1)(b): full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)`

-- For the purposes of paragraph (a) and no limit: yes.
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not for the purposes of paragraph (a): the grant does not reach it, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Each limit alone, with the purpose met.
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 23(1)(b) the company has full rights, powers and privileges for the purposes of paragraph (a)` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 23(1A) and (1B): objects and restrictions in the constitution`

-- A provision stating the objects of the company: the company may have it in its constitution.
#ASSERT `s 23(1A) the company may have its objects included in its constitution` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Some other provision: the subsection is silent.
#ASSERT `s 23(1A) the company may have its objects included in its constitution` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- A provision restricting capacity, rights, powers or privileges: the constitution may contain it.
#ASSERT `s 23(1B) the constitution may contain the provision` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 23(1B) the constitution may contain the provision` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 24: provision for employees on a cessation of business`

-- Both facts: the company's powers are deemed to include the power.
#ASSERT `s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Provision not in connection with a cessation of business, or not for employees: the deeming does not reach it.
#ASSERT `s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 24(1) the powers of the company are deemed to include power to make the provision` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 24(2): where the constitution requires approval in general meeting or prescribes the manner, subsection (1) does not affect it.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) subsection (1) affects the constitution's provision on how the power is exercised` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Where the constitution has no such provision, subsection (2) has nothing to say.
#ASSERT `s 24(2) subsection (1) affects the constitution's provision on how the power is exercised` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
